    <p><strong>We are not responsible for the privacy, security, accuracy, availability, or practices of third-party websites, platforms, or service providers, except to the extent required by applicable law</strong>.</p>
    <p><strong>6. Payments, Deposits, and Fees</strong></p>
    <p>Fees for services are listed on the website, booking platform, or otherwise communicated to you before or at the time of service. Prices are subject to change unless you have already booked and received confirmation for a specific service at a specific price.</p>
    <p>We may require payment, a deposit, or a valid payment card to schedule or hold an appointment. By providing payment information, you authorize the applicable charges for services, deposits, cancellation fees, no-show fees, or other charges disclosed to you.</p>
    <p><strong>7. Cancellation, Rescheduling, and No-Show Policy</strong></p>
    <p>Appointments require advance planning and reserved time. Unless otherwise stated in writing:</p>
    <p>Clients must cancel or reschedule at least <strong>24 hours</strong> before the scheduled appointment time. Cancellations or rescheduling requests made after that deadline may be subject to a cancellation fee of  <strong>50% of service price</strong>.</p>
    <p>Clients who do not appear for a scheduled appointment may be charged a no-show fee of <strong>100% of service price</strong>.</p>
    <p>We reserve the right to waive fees at our discretion, including for emergencies or circumstances beyond a client’s control.</p>
    <p><strong>8. Late Arrival Policy</strong></p>
    <p>If you arrive late, your session may be shortened to avoid delaying other clients. You may still be responsible for the full scheduled service fee. If you arrive too late for the service to be safely or reasonably performed, the appointment may be treated as a late cancellation or no-show.</p>
    <p><strong>9. Client Conduct and Professional Boundaries</strong></p>
    <p>Massage therapy is a professional service. Clients must behave respectfully and appropriately at all times.</p>
    <p>Sexual comments, sexual conduct, harassment, threats, discriminatory behavior, intoxication, unsafe conduct, or inappropriate requests will not be tolerated. We reserve the right to immediately end a session, refuse service, charge the full service fee, and decline future appointments if a client violates professional boundaries or creates an unsafe or inappropriate environment.</p>
    <p><strong>10. Right to Refuse or Discontinue Service</strong></p>
    <p>We reserve the right to refuse, postpone, modify, or discontinue services when we determine, in our professional judgment, that massage therapy may be unsafe, inappropriate, contraindicated, or inconsistent with professional standards.</p>
    <p>This may include, but is not limited to, situations involving illness, fever, contagious conditions, skin infections, open wounds, intoxication, unsafe behavior, undisclosed medical issues, or failure to complete required intake forms.</p>
    <p><strong>11. Minors</strong></p>
    <p>Clients under 18 years old must have consent from a parent or legal guardian before receiving services. A parent or legal guardian may be required to remain present during the appointment, depending on the service, the client’s age, and business policy.</p>
